WEBVTT

00:00:18.051 --> 00:00:22.088
Though you are so close,
Kore hodo soba ni

00:00:22.088 --> 00:00:26.593
I cannot tell you how I feel.
Iru no ni tsutaerarezu

00:00:26.593 --> 00:00:30.663
The more strongly I feel,
Tsuyoku omou hodo

00:00:30.663 --> 00:00:35.268
the harder it is for me to find the words.
Kotoba ga mitsukaranai

00:00:35.268 --> 00:00:43.309
What is sad is not fate...
Kanashii no wa unmei ja nakute

00:00:43.309 --> 00:00:54.083
...but that all encounters come to an end.
Deai no subete ni owari ga aru koto

00:00:54.487 --> 00:00:58.525
O incomplete beings,
Mikan naru mono

00:00:58.525 --> 00:01:02.962
awaken, for beyond the night...
mezameyo yoru o koetara

00:01:02.962 --> 00:01:07.033
At the end of the desert...
Sabaku no hate ni

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:14.701
...the truth surely awaits you.
Shinjitsu ga matteru yo kitto

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:44.296
"O star, as thy dream dictates,"

00:01:44.838 --> 00:01:47.272
"Let us depart on a journey tonight."

00:01:48.074 --> 00:01:51.566
"In the embrace of the blue night sky,
the whispering wind,"

00:01:51.978 --> 00:01:55.482
"and the blessing of the children
that dwell upon the land."

00:01:55.482 --> 00:01:56.039
Honoka.

00:01:57.550 --> 00:02:01.111
Donna Myfree's poems are all
fine and good, but soon...

00:02:01.254 --> 00:02:04.246
I know. It's coming into view for me, too.

00:02:32.819 --> 00:02:37.688
The Story That Begins Here

00:02:55.141 --> 00:02:58.440
If you were going to greet us,
you could've come in person.

00:02:58.611 --> 00:03:01.548
Unfortunately, depending on your response,

00:03:01.548 --> 00:03:04.346
we have to move on to our next
course of action right away.

00:03:05.351 --> 00:03:06.409
Course of action, huh?

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:09.315
Turn back immediately.

00:03:09.589 --> 00:03:12.854
Your action infringes upon the Technos Taboo.

00:03:13.393 --> 00:03:15.128
I know that.

00:03:15.128 --> 00:03:18.298
If you obey this order now and withdraw,

00:03:18.298 --> 00:03:20.333
your actions thus far will be overlooked.

00:03:20.333 --> 00:03:21.732
I have no intention of obeying.

00:03:23.169 --> 00:03:24.727
Tell me why.

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:29.500
Screw you, Technos Taboo!

00:03:30.076 --> 00:03:31.202
That's all.

00:03:31.578 --> 00:03:33.341
A simple answer.

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:34.539
And you?

00:03:35.548 --> 00:03:38.418
My objective in coming to this planet...

00:03:38.418 --> 00:03:41.921
...was none other than to make my way here.

00:03:41.921 --> 00:03:44.048
My withdrawing from this
place is an impossibility.

00:03:44.657 --> 00:03:46.056
What is here?

00:03:46.326 --> 00:03:49.056
That, you must know as well as I.

00:03:49.462 --> 00:03:52.226
Isn't what you're going to
do first pretty much set?

00:03:52.665 --> 00:03:54.997
Why don't you start with the
opponent that's easier to fight?

00:03:55.168 --> 00:03:56.100
Miss Honoka...

00:03:56.202 --> 00:03:57.066
Don't say anything, Iks.

00:03:57.870 --> 00:04:03.069
I think it's probably the best
choice for both Joganki and me.

00:04:05.411 --> 00:04:07.247
This isn't the time for indecision.

00:04:07.247 --> 00:04:10.876
I've come to willfully break the Technos Taboo.

00:04:13.253 --> 00:04:14.413
You're right.

00:04:32.238 --> 00:04:33.364
Honoka, out of the way!

00:04:33.539 --> 00:04:35.029
This is my department!

00:04:35.275 --> 00:04:37.175
Bogie, I don't need your help.

00:04:37.277 --> 00:04:38.144
Leave it to me.

00:04:38.144 --> 00:04:39.008
Honoka!

00:04:39.479 --> 00:04:42.175
Please Iks, you too. Wait here.

00:06:07.667 --> 00:06:10.966
Miss Honoka's abilities have clearly evolved.

00:06:11.704 --> 00:06:14.502
The infusion of regenerative
cells that Kamui gave her...

00:06:15.041 --> 00:06:17.202
...have drawn out her powers...

00:06:29.622 --> 00:06:31.351
Why are you taking us down?!

00:06:31.557 --> 00:06:33.192
I am going to see him.

00:06:33.192 --> 00:06:34.386
What for?!

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:36.685
You don't mean to take him
to the Singularity, do you?!

00:06:37.029 --> 00:06:41.667
Joganki, the underlying issue
is not just the Technos Taboo!

00:06:41.667 --> 00:06:42.691
Surely, you know that!

00:06:44.971 --> 00:06:47.701
When he arrives at the Singularity,

00:06:48.141 --> 00:06:51.043
what will be conducted there
and what will happen?

00:06:51.043 --> 00:06:53.671
We cannot even begin to predict those things!

00:06:54.147 --> 00:06:56.012
So we must stop him at all costs!

00:06:56.082 --> 00:06:58.017
With what means would we stop him?

00:06:58.017 --> 00:07:00.086
Given this situation against Honoka alone.

00:07:00.086 --> 00:07:00.711
But...

00:07:01.087 --> 00:07:05.958
If The Third's military might leads to
excessive destruction and losses,

00:07:05.958 --> 00:07:07.550
we would be no different than humans.

00:07:16.602 --> 00:07:18.263
The Steel Gorge.

00:07:19.105 --> 00:07:22.040
A great ravine located at the
center of the Rokugo Desert.

00:07:23.142 --> 00:07:26.846
This fissure in the land that runs
interminably to the east and west...

00:07:26.846 --> 00:07:28.815
...is as if the planet itself...

00:07:28.815 --> 00:07:33.718
...has left a never-closing wound
exposed for all to see.

00:07:36.322 --> 00:07:41.060
As a Class 1 top secret location,

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:43.996
The Third have it under
extremely tight security...

00:07:43.996 --> 00:07:46.988
...in order to make sure
not a soul comes near it.

00:08:19.765 --> 00:08:22.602
We call this place the Singularity,
and since the beginning,

00:08:22.602 --> 00:08:26.766
we have been aware of the being lying
dormant at the bottom of the gorge.

00:08:27.507 --> 00:08:31.170
A body of energy thought to hold an
overwhelming amount of potential.

00:08:31.577 --> 00:08:35.206
Its existence was nothing but a threat...

00:08:35.781 --> 00:08:37.717
...and successive generations of The Third...

00:08:37.717 --> 00:08:40.753
...have used every conceivable means...

00:08:40.753 --> 00:08:43.051
...in an attempt to communicate
with this being in some way.

00:08:43.756 --> 00:08:45.424
The accumulated result of that...

00:08:45.424 --> 00:08:48.261
The various technologies and legacies
from the past to the present...

00:08:48.261 --> 00:08:49.489
...can be found here.

00:08:51.397 --> 00:08:54.133
You feared the outflow of the technology here...

00:08:54.133 --> 00:08:58.297
Is that why you limited access to this
place with the Technos Taboo?

00:08:58.404 --> 00:09:00.706
It is true, that was one reason,

00:09:00.706 --> 00:09:04.938
but we were also afraid of the
being that lies dormant down there.

00:09:05.411 --> 00:09:06.605
We realized...

00:09:06.979 --> 00:09:10.039
...that it was not us
who had been monitoring him,

00:09:10.182 --> 00:09:13.208
but that he had been monitoring us.

00:09:14.253 --> 00:09:16.551
What is this "he"?

00:09:16.789 --> 00:09:20.782
The only one in our world who
knows the answer to that is...

00:09:24.363 --> 00:09:28.493
I have feared that this day
would come someday.

00:09:28.834 --> 00:09:29.630
But...

00:09:31.637 --> 00:09:35.869
I now think that perhaps part of
me had been hoping it would.

00:09:43.549 --> 00:09:46.643
The territory beyond this point
has been completely untouchable.

00:09:46.719 --> 00:09:50.256
Not even powerful thought, to say
nothing of physical technologies,

00:09:50.256 --> 00:09:52.747
has been able to penetrate past this point.

00:09:53.693 --> 00:09:54.387
Let's go.

00:09:54.827 --> 00:09:55.486
What?

00:09:56.262 --> 00:09:59.925
Please synchronize with my
thoughts as much as possible.

00:10:20.186 --> 00:10:21.118
This place...

00:10:23.756 --> 00:10:26.247
Have we entered into his domain?

00:10:27.326 --> 00:10:28.691
I have been waiting.

00:10:30.096 --> 00:10:31.620
This voice is...

00:10:32.264 --> 00:10:35.062
It has been long. It has been long.

00:10:35.735 --> 00:10:37.303
O Observer,

00:10:37.303 --> 00:10:40.067
I must apologize to you.

00:10:40.773 --> 00:10:43.241
Have I been forsaken?

00:10:43.709 --> 00:10:46.946
The things that I have done upon this
land, the things that I have seen.

00:10:46.946 --> 00:10:49.676
Was it all meaningless?

00:10:50.383 --> 00:10:53.052
This... emotion...

00:10:53.052 --> 00:10:55.350
Sorrow? Despair?

00:10:55.488 --> 00:10:57.979
No, it's more hollow...

00:10:59.291 --> 00:10:59.985
Nihility!

00:11:01.160 --> 00:11:03.094
It is true, then?

00:11:03.162 --> 00:11:04.530
I can understand...

00:11:04.530 --> 00:11:07.966
...the meaning of the judgment
that is likely to be handed down.

00:11:09.335 --> 00:11:10.970
O Observer,

00:11:10.970 --> 00:11:14.030
before that, show me what you have seen.

00:11:16.442 --> 00:11:18.501
I am prepared to accept it.

00:11:19.245 --> 00:11:20.542
Very well.

00:11:36.362 --> 00:11:37.192
Who?

00:11:38.064 --> 00:11:40.225
Who was it that was born?

00:11:41.267 --> 00:11:42.234
You?

00:11:43.369 --> 00:11:44.529
Me?

00:11:52.645 --> 00:11:54.613
This is me...

00:11:56.916 --> 00:11:59.111
The things that begin in me...

00:12:00.286 --> 00:12:02.584
The things that trace back to me...

00:12:03.856 --> 00:12:05.517
The things that are me.

00:12:06.826 --> 00:12:08.594
I have watched this planet...

00:12:08.594 --> 00:12:13.429
...and the rise and fall of the
intelligence that was born here.

00:12:14.667 --> 00:12:21.402
I have merely kept watch over the
evolution of life and of intelligence.

00:12:22.808 --> 00:12:28.371
The intelligence on this planet
seemed to hold wonderful potential.

00:12:29.381 --> 00:12:30.473
However...

00:12:35.955 --> 00:12:37.149
Why?

00:12:38.090 --> 00:12:39.387
The hate...

00:12:39.959 --> 00:12:40.926
The rage...

00:12:41.694 --> 00:12:43.161
They envelop me.

00:12:44.663 --> 00:12:45.755
Why?

00:12:46.899 --> 00:12:49.424
I am burned in blazing flames.

00:12:50.636 --> 00:12:53.264
All that was built crumbles.

00:12:53.939 --> 00:12:55.065
But...

00:12:55.341 --> 00:12:58.777
...the one who pulled that trigger is also me.

00:12:59.845 --> 00:13:02.177
All was lost.

00:13:03.449 --> 00:13:05.785
The things that disappear...

00:13:05.785 --> 00:13:07.946
The things that begin in me...

00:13:08.487 --> 00:13:10.512
The things that trace back to me...

00:13:11.357 --> 00:13:12.517
It hurts.

00:13:12.792 --> 00:13:15.317
It's so painful and so cold...

00:13:26.906 --> 00:13:28.931
Are these... tears?

00:13:29.775 --> 00:13:34.109
The emotions... The trembling
of my heart... They won't stop.

00:13:36.682 --> 00:13:38.206
We saw the same things...

00:13:38.317 --> 00:13:40.547
No, experienced them, didn't we?

00:13:42.788 --> 00:13:44.016
That just now...

00:13:44.223 --> 00:13:45.952
What I felt just now...

00:13:47.927 --> 00:13:49.895
Did you feel it?

00:13:49.895 --> 00:13:53.558
The grief and pain that pierced my being.

00:13:54.166 --> 00:13:55.599
O Arbiter.

00:13:57.770 --> 00:13:59.138
Arbiter?

00:13:59.138 --> 00:14:00.172
In all likelihood,

00:14:00.172 --> 00:14:05.701
Arbiter Iks and this voice,
the Observer, came from the same place.

00:14:05.878 --> 00:14:08.574
The Observer, in the distant past.

00:14:09.048 --> 00:14:12.074
O Arbiter, everything has already...

00:14:12.852 --> 00:14:17.056
No, ultimately, I am one who merely observes.

00:14:17.056 --> 00:14:18.489
I will say no more.

00:14:18.724 --> 00:14:20.885
Please continue, Observer.

00:14:21.293 --> 00:14:23.318
Do you believe that all is over?

00:14:23.729 --> 00:14:27.825
That there is nothing more that
will spring anew from this place?

00:14:29.568 --> 00:14:30.830
I...

00:14:53.993 --> 00:14:55.327
I...

00:14:55.327 --> 00:14:56.123
Wait!

00:14:58.864 --> 00:14:59.956
I'm sorry.

00:15:00.366 --> 00:15:02.459
I'm truly sorry.

00:15:03.602 --> 00:15:04.466
Miss Honoka?

00:15:05.170 --> 00:15:07.606
Girl, whose name I do not even know.

00:15:07.606 --> 00:15:11.599
What is it that you have ever done to me?

00:15:11.810 --> 00:15:13.744
I-I...

00:15:14.446 --> 00:15:16.971
Perhaps that would be better.

00:15:17.716 --> 00:15:21.482
Better if you speak to the Observer,
Miss Honoka.

00:15:22.187 --> 00:15:23.154
Iks...

00:15:25.190 --> 00:15:27.351
You, who live upon this planet.

00:15:29.361 --> 00:15:32.125
For a long... long time, I've felt it.

00:15:32.731 --> 00:15:34.130
Your soul.

00:15:34.633 --> 00:15:38.399
The sorrow, the pain, the suffering...

00:15:38.804 --> 00:15:44.640
That your soul had gone beyond
emotions and become empty...

00:15:45.044 --> 00:15:47.638
Girl, do you know?

00:15:47.780 --> 00:15:51.341
The horror of only being able to watch?

00:15:51.417 --> 00:15:54.716
The horror of being unable to do anything?

00:15:55.321 --> 00:15:56.822
Even so...

00:15:56.822 --> 00:16:00.019
Even so, you continued to watch over us, right?

00:16:00.726 --> 00:16:03.092
That's why I want to apologize.

00:16:03.329 --> 00:16:08.467
If everyone had realized that
you were watching over them,

00:16:08.467 --> 00:16:11.027
something might have been different.

00:16:11.270 --> 00:16:14.139
Are you saying that the
mere act of my watching...

00:16:14.139 --> 00:16:18.166
...could have meant something
to all of you as well?

00:16:19.878 --> 00:16:23.473
That what I have done was not for naught...

00:16:24.616 --> 00:16:29.144
I think it can't be helped, no matter
what answer you come up with now.

00:16:29.221 --> 00:16:34.352
Because we've subjected you to
so much grief and suffering.

00:16:35.327 --> 00:16:36.316
But...

00:16:36.595 --> 00:16:38.825
That's exactly why I want to say this!

00:16:38.964 --> 00:16:41.933
To you, who've watched over us all this time!

00:16:43.168 --> 00:16:44.931
To say, "Thank you."

00:16:51.477 --> 00:16:52.637
Observer?

00:16:54.246 --> 00:16:55.679
O girl.

00:16:56.382 --> 00:16:58.714
O kindhearted girl,

00:16:58.984 --> 00:17:01.452
I should be the one to thank you.

00:17:02.354 --> 00:17:03.150
What?

00:17:03.455 --> 00:17:06.253
You have cried for my sake.

00:17:06.325 --> 00:17:08.725
You have embraced my soul.

00:17:09.328 --> 00:17:11.660
Thank you, girl.

00:17:17.369 --> 00:17:21.237
Terror suddenly gripped Honoka's heart.

00:17:22.207 --> 00:17:24.109
As if she had only just realized...

00:17:24.109 --> 00:17:27.079
...the extraordinary magnitude of
the being she had just spoken with...

00:17:27.079 --> 00:17:29.411
...and what they had spoken of.

00:17:32.818 --> 00:17:34.115
O Observer,

00:17:34.586 --> 00:17:36.388
in her time before coming here,

00:17:36.388 --> 00:17:40.484
she has watched over, embraced,
and comforted many a soul.

00:17:41.527 --> 00:17:44.830
The soul of a weapon that
had been abandoned...

00:17:44.830 --> 00:17:48.493
...and lost sight of his reason for being,
shedding tears like a lonely boy...

00:17:49.535 --> 00:17:51.503
The soul of a little girl,
who was in turmoil at the gap...

00:17:52.237 --> 00:17:55.035
...between what she aspired to
be and who she was in reality.

00:17:56.208 --> 00:17:59.778
A soul that agonized at the
love she could not convey.

00:17:59.778 --> 00:18:01.246
And the other soul,

00:18:01.246 --> 00:18:03.449
whose fate it was to inherit her soul...

00:18:03.449 --> 00:18:05.280
...and do as she had done.

00:18:06.718 --> 00:18:10.522
That is why I think it is now my
turn to be the one to embrace...

00:18:10.522 --> 00:18:11.989
...Miss Honoka's soul.

00:18:13.192 --> 00:18:14.022
Iks...

00:18:15.227 --> 00:18:19.186
By doing so, I believe I can
learn more about this planet...

00:18:19.865 --> 00:18:24.564
Learn more about the life that
breathes upon this planet.

00:18:25.404 --> 00:18:27.573
In meeting Miss Honoka,

00:18:27.573 --> 00:18:31.543
I have begun to feel that humans
have once again begun to think...

00:18:31.543 --> 00:18:35.980
...about what it means to live and
what the true nature of life is.

00:18:36.949 --> 00:18:39.747
O Arbiter, does that mean...

00:18:39.918 --> 00:18:42.079
Let's wait and see a little longer.

00:18:42.187 --> 00:18:44.178
The arbitration can still be done then.

00:18:44.623 --> 00:18:48.059
I will take on your role from now on.

00:18:49.194 --> 00:18:53.722
I am grateful, Arbiter. And, girl...

00:18:55.267 --> 00:19:01.536
It was my salvation to have met the
human that you are at the very end.

00:19:09.181 --> 00:19:10.079
Kamui!

00:19:33.539 --> 00:19:35.530
Iks, the Fairy...

00:19:36.408 --> 00:19:38.376
Her time to depart has come.

00:19:38.911 --> 00:19:42.142
The Fairy departs together with the Observer.

00:19:42.447 --> 00:19:44.381
The Fairy must have also been uncertain.

00:19:45.117 --> 00:19:49.254
Whether or not it was a good thing
to scatter the genetic information...

00:19:49.254 --> 00:19:51.490
...of this planet across the universe.

00:19:51.490 --> 00:19:52.324
But...

00:19:52.324 --> 00:19:54.918
She's decided to depart, hasn't she?

00:19:55.160 --> 00:19:57.128
The Fairy's decided that it's all right, too!

00:20:02.734 --> 00:20:04.224
Do not forget.

00:20:04.770 --> 00:20:08.001
You are me. I am you.

00:20:08.941 --> 00:20:12.570
Though we may be far apart,
remember that much.

00:20:12.711 --> 00:20:14.576
Never forget it.

00:20:14.646 --> 00:20:15.943
I won't forget...

00:20:16.248 --> 00:20:17.146
I won't forget it!

00:20:25.190 --> 00:20:26.248
The Fairy...

00:20:26.358 --> 00:20:27.655
The Fairy's departing on her journey!

00:20:31.330 --> 00:20:33.662
Among humans and The Third,

00:20:33.765 --> 00:20:35.434
with the exception of the Technos Taboo,

00:20:35.434 --> 00:20:39.165
it has been like an unwritten rule
that we stay clear of one another.

00:20:39.972 --> 00:20:44.033
But perhaps her existence will change that.

00:20:44.409 --> 00:20:47.713
As a third being, in the true sense of the word,

00:20:47.713 --> 00:20:49.681
who will be the link between
humans and The Third.

00:20:50.949 --> 00:20:52.610
Perhaps so.

00:20:52.985 --> 00:20:56.682
But I'm sure Miss Honoka would say,
"I am who I am."

00:20:57.556 --> 00:21:01.993
Perhaps there is a need to reconsider
the Technos Taboo as well.

00:21:02.227 --> 00:21:04.058
Miss Honoka will be happy to hear that.

00:21:06.798 --> 00:21:09.494
We'll meet again! That's a promise!

00:21:44.536 --> 00:21:48.473
That night, people saw the blue light...

00:21:48.473 --> 00:21:51.306
...and for some reason, were moved to prayer.

00:21:52.511 --> 00:21:56.607
Wishing that no matter where
the light was journeying to,

00:21:57.282 --> 00:22:01.116
the new future would not err in its path this time.

00:22:03.422 --> 00:22:06.721
"And the blessing of the children
that dwell upon this land,"

00:22:07.292 --> 00:22:09.157
"if you are truly fortunate,"

00:22:09.728 --> 00:22:13.129
"the tomorrow you arrive at will be kind."

00:22:20.939 --> 00:22:25.205
"All will begin here, and all will return here."
"All will begin here, and all will return here."

00:22:29.081 --> 00:22:30.349
Joganki?

00:22:30.349 --> 00:22:31.373
He...

00:22:31.750 --> 00:22:33.618
Iks, in the presence of the Observer,

00:22:33.618 --> 00:22:36.815
audaciously proclaimed his
own feelings for Honoka.

00:22:37.522 --> 00:22:38.819
His own feelings?

00:22:39.491 --> 00:22:42.324
If that wasn't a confession of love,
I don't know what is.

00:22:43.362 --> 00:22:45.489
What a plebian thing to say.

00:22:45.597 --> 00:22:49.334
But if so, that means you've lost, does it not?

00:22:49.334 --> 00:22:50.266
Lost?

00:22:50.535 --> 00:22:53.561
Now, that is a truly plebian
thing to say, Fila Marique.

00:22:54.106 --> 00:22:55.403
Is that so?

00:22:56.241 --> 00:22:58.038
Then I shall not sympathize.

00:23:03.014 --> 00:23:04.606
Sorry for making you wait, Bogie.

00:23:05.016 --> 00:23:05.812
Did you worry?

00:23:06.051 --> 00:23:08.387
If I worried over every little incident like this,

00:23:08.387 --> 00:23:09.820
I couldn't be your partner.

00:23:10.155 --> 00:23:11.713
Come on, we're leaving.

00:23:11.823 --> 00:23:12.414
Yeah.

00:23:12.858 --> 00:23:13.950
Let's go, Iks!

00:23:14.192 --> 00:23:15.761
I'll show you more!

00:23:15.761 --> 00:23:18.059
Everything that I know of this world!

00:23:19.264 --> 00:23:19.992
Yes.
